Vendor-provided vector algorithms exposed in this environment include HNSW, IVF and DiskANN (the cluster advertises DiskANN, HNSW and IVF). Index creation uses the MongoDB createIndex interface with a vector index spec. Example (adapt to actual driver API):
db.transactions.createIndex(
  { embedding: "vector" },
  { vector: { dimensions: 1536, algorithm: "hnsw", distanceMetric: "cosine", m: 16, efConstruction: 200 } }
)
(Replace dimensions and algorithm parameters to match your embedding size and desired algorithm.)

Use the mongodb driver and read connection URI from process.env.DOCUMENTDB_URI. Example connection code:
const { MongoClient } = require('mongodb');
const client = new MongoClient(process.env.DOCUMENTDB_URI, { useNewUrlParser: true, useUnifiedTopology: true });
await client.connect();
const db = client.db('sample_fintech_02');
// then use db.collection('transactions')
Do not embed the URI in code; use .env.example with a placeholder.
